tag_name = "v2.0.0"
release_name = "MCLI v2.0.0 - SUI, IKA, Walrus and IOTA validator toolkit in Rust"
body = """
## What's New

### IKA validators
- `mcli ika status` - validators whose commission caps your keys hold, with the commission ready to collect
- `mcli ika collect` - collect commission of every validator in one run (`--validator`, `--to`, `--amount`)
- `mcli ika send` - move IKA from a validator account

### Walrus storage nodes
- `mcli walrus status` - nodes whose commission your keys receive, with the part ready to collect and the part locked until the epoch's voting ends
- `mcli walrus collect` - collect commission of every node in one transaction (`--node`, `--to`); works when the receiver is an address or the node's `StorageNodeCap`
- `mcli walrus send` - move WAL from a node account

### Keys in one place, no profile switching
- Private keys live in `~/.mcli/.env` (`SUI_PRIVATE_KEY`, `IOTA_PRIVATE_KEY`, `IKA_PRIVATE_KEY_<N>`, `WALRUS_PRIVATE_KEY`); the file must be `chmod 600`
- The tool signs transactions itself: the `sui` and `iota` binaries and their active profiles are no longer needed

### Interactive menu
- Run `mcli` without arguments to pick the chain, action and account from menus

### Rewritten in Rust
- SUI uses gRPC through the official Mysten Rust SDK (Mysten full nodes no longer serve JSON-RPC)
- `withdraw-all` withdraws every stake, rewards included, in a single transaction (SUI goes to the address balance, IOTA arrives as one coin)
- `send` executes the transfer instead of printing a script
- Every transaction is simulated and shown before signing; `--dry-run` and `--address` allow read-only runs
- Transactions built by the RPC node are checked before signing: sender, called packages and recipients

### Breaking Changes
- `--amount` is in whole coins (`12.5`), not MIST/NANOS
- Config moved from `~/.mcli-config/config.toml` to `~/.mcli/config.toml`; addresses come from the keys
- Run `mcli init` to create the new config and the `.env` template
"""
